Enhancement: Add `--proxy-headers` option for use behind a reverse proxy

Rest-server now supports the `--proxy-headers` option. When enabled, the
client address is taken from proxy headers such as `X-Forwarded-For`, so the
log shows the real client IP address instead of the address of the reverse
proxy. The option is disabled by default and should only be enabled when
rest-server is reachable exclusively through a trusted proxy.

https://github.com/restic/rest-server/issues/233
